      "writtenOn": "2025-09-25T13:12:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I am opening to removing our custom sorts given that `std::sort` outperforms our variants. `std::sort` also has specialized block quick sort implementations for 32-bit and 64-bit integer types that it will use automatically, which are particularly fast.\n\nThe +10kb code size is unfortunate, but it looks like some of it is still referencing various SkT[x]Sort functions so perhaps just removing SkTSort.h entirely would be the way to go.",
